                            WORLD OF WARCRAFT GUIDES AND MANUALS



                     I have enjoyed playing WOW for about three years
now.
                   I had four or five alts, that is players in
different
                   realms.Because of this I was playing them all and
                   keeping them at about the same level.The game was
therefore
                   different for all my characters as was the learning
experience.
                   Most of my characters were of a different
class.Also I did not
                   join a guild and had no information or help with
the game
                   experience or quest.
                     Now that being said,I developed a sort of pride
and
                   confidence that many players don,t have.Abilities
to escape and
                   and avoid trouble were learned at these lower
levels. finding
                   chests and objects were also a learned ability.
Even though
                   knowledge of where things are ahead of time was a
jealousy
                   I had to live with.
                     My point is this: I found playing WOW only with
guides
                   and manuals detracted from the overall sence of
accomplishment
                   and fun of the game.
                     I spent many hours playiong WOW without even
realizing the
                   vast resourses of the auction houses.Again we have
the discussion
                   of guilds and manuals.First we know all about
"twinks". Twinks
                   are players who use real money to buy large amounts
of gold.
                   They can buy the best equipment and supplies and in
so doing
                   are set apart from the rest of the players.
                     There are choices to make in the game of WOW. Are
you
                   interested or have the playing time to develope
your
                   character at the basic game pace or will you decide
to "twink"? How
                   much or when will you chose to use the guides and
manuals or
                   even pay real money for "twink
gold"?
                     I haven,t disscused thottbot.com and wowwiki.com.
but I will
                   now.Let me ask ypou the question again. How much
playing time
                   are you willing to spend? Where does the enjoyment
of leveling
                   in trade and character end? How does one balance
outside resources
                   with game enjoyment? That is the main question a
player should ask
                   him or her self as they are playing.
                     It was fun for me and I had the playing time to
level up with
                   almost no help at all. However around level 40 or
so I got a game
                   manual and started using it for maps and
information quite often.
                   My gaming experience became more fun and the pace
picked up. My
                   opinion is I needed a manual to keep me interested
in the game.
                   Basic game play was outmoded for me around level
40. With others
                   the game may slow down at level 20 or lower. I
guess one could
                   compare outside aids as a health potion. At
somepoint a player
                   must "get his health" back to continue the game.
                     I was very proud never to have used outside aids
but like I said
                   I need the health food! Thottbot and Wowwiki are
search engines
                   easily found on the internet. They give almost any
wow topic a
                   facts and discussion.Also included are players own
comments that
                   cover almost any question. Personally at around
level 50 or so I
                   "gave in" and started using thottbot.com and
wowwiki com. They are
                   used by everyone at that level.Again a more potent"
health food"
                   and my gaming experience was much more fun and the
pace much faster.
                   When to use those search engines again is a matter
for of one's
                   own taste.
                     Finally is a vast game of many player
interactions and game
                   interactions and subtleties. Use outside resources
when you need to
                   but don't ruin the game before you have actually
started. Again pay
                   for gold level up and destroy everything in your
path if that is
                   the kind of game you like to play! Good luck and
enjoy anyway you
